      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PHOENIX REX (5) maintained his perfect record when he ventured north for a G2 win at Albion Park last start. His other three victories each came at this venue, drawing wider than this and racing three deep without cover but proving too tough two back. The one to beat. INSULATOR (1) improved to place when second-up at this circuit and distance last start, coming from this barrier to get within 3.6m of the unbeaten Verbici. Could progress further with added fitness. WHERDASUNDONTSHINE (2) is a colt by Majestic Son on debut for Jess Tubbs. Has been trialling well and a nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Keep safe. SUMTHIN DIFFERENT (7) has had two months off since a G2 placing at Menangle last start but has been kept up to the mark with two trials, winning the latest.",
